+    $$ gi_2 = perm[ii + i_2 + perm[jj + j_2 + perm[kk + k_2]]] \ \& \ 11 $$
+    $$ gi_3 = perm[ii + 1 + perm[jj + 1 + perm[kk + 1]]] \ \& \ 11 $$
+    
+    Retrieve the gradient vectors:
+    $$ \mathbf{g}_0 = grad3[gi_0] $$
+    $$ \mathbf{g}_1 = grad3[gi_1] $$
+    $$ \mathbf{g}_2 = grad3[gi_2] $$
+    $$ \mathbf{g}_3 = grad3[gi_3] $$
+
+6.  **Contribution Calculation:**
+    For each corner $m \in \{0, 1, 2, 3\}$ with relative coordinate $\mathbf{x}_m$ and gradient $\mathbf{g}_m$:
+    $$ t_m = C_{cut} - (\mathbf{x}_m \cdot \mathbf{x}_m) $$
+    If $t_m < 0$, the contribution $n_m = 0$.
+    Otherwise:
+    $$ n_m = t_m^4 \times (\mathbf{g}_m \cdot \mathbf{x}_m) $$
+    *(Note: $t_m^4$ is computed as $(t_m^2)^2$)*
+
+7.  **Final Result:**
+    Sum the contributions and scale:
+    $$ N = S \times (n_0 + n_1 + n_2 + n_3) $$
 
